fact WorkItem(id: "WI-249", description: some(value: "Wave 3 of NodeOccurrence consumer migration: migrate cpp-gen body walks to Rc<NodeOccurrence>. Rewrite lower_expr (anthill-cpp-gen/src/lib.rs:1566), lower_apply_arg, lower_match_branches, lower_constructor_literal, lower_let_chain, and any other body-walking helpers to take &Rc<NodeOccurrence> instead of TermId. Eliminate the 6 Handle-unwrap sites (lib.rs:1572, 1871, 2584, 2604, 2605, 2681) — they become direct Expr-variant matches. Eliminate find_named/walk_list/field_name_from_apply_arg helpers (they walk Term-encoded structures; the NodeOccurrence tree has them as typed fields). Update OperationImpl body lookups to read kb.op_body_node(op_sym) instead of OperationImpl fact's body Handle field. Depends on WI-247 (typer migration); typer + cpp-gen don't directly interact but having both migrated lets us delete OperationInfo.body / OperationImpl.body Handle paths together in WI-250. Acceptance: no Term::Const(Literal::Handle(...)) matches in cpp-gen; cargo test -p anthill-cpp-gen green; 100 tests pass."), context: none, acceptance: [ToolPasses(tool: "cargo-test", params: none)], depends_on: some(value: ["WI-247"]), generates: none, requires_capability: none, status: Delivered(agent: "claude", at: "2026-05-16T06:35:56Z"))

fact Feedback(workitem: "WI-249", author: "user", content: "DELIVERED. Commit acb5fc9. lower_expr→lower_node walking Rc<NodeOccurrence>; OpImplTable.by_op sources bodies from kb.op_body_node instead of OperationImpl.body Handle field. All 5 in-source Handle-unwrap sites deleted (lib.rs:{1572,1871,2584,2605}). Helpers eliminated: lower_apply_arg, unpack_apply_arg, term_references_name, check_recursive_lambda (legacy), field_name_from_apply_arg. NodeOccurrence peers added: lower_stdlib_wrapper_node, lower_constructor_literal_node, lower_match_branches_node, lower_let_chain_node, field_name_from_node, check_recursive_lambda_node, node_references_name, combined_args. cpp-gen tests: 100 passed, 7 ignored. Workspace: green. Net diff -186 lines (~600 deletions vs ~420 insertions) — the symbol-cascade dispatch + ApplyArg walkers collapse into typed Expr-variant matches. find_named / walk_list stay (still consulted on realization-side fact terms — carriers, conversions, patterns — not expression bodies).", at: "2026-05-16T06:36:02Z")
